    "//#lint:e2e:fix": {
      "description": "Root-level task: ESLint --fix over e2e/. Mutates the source tree, so cache:false -- a cache replay could restore stale content. Companion to //#lint:e2e; local/manual invocation, NEVER wired into a gate, because a gate must verify and not rewrite (same contract as //#lint:scripts:fix). Exists because e2e/ went unlinted for the life of the repo -- @fleet/e2e declares only a typecheck script, so the package-scoped lint task never reached it -- and the first run of //#lint:e2e reported 35 violations, 25 of them mechanically fixable. Fixing in bulk is deliberately followed by READING THE DIFF: an unreviewed --fix across two dozen spec files could silently alter test semantics, and 2026 guidance is explicit that a blanket --fix over a whole tree is the wrong move even with a sound fixer. cache:false. Run: pnpm exec turbo run lint:e2e:fix.",
